  "scope": "The actual self-delimited source reader allocates three primitive two-word tables in sequence; an actual recursive first-column projection creates the original-order matrix spine from the same decoded word cells. The same physical run starts from an empty heap, preserves the source suffix, emits every exact request event and pays its terminal halt within an original-input linear instruction bound and full bit-machine simulation bound. Capacity-field and demand-occurrence contracts refer to the actual decoded cells, including duplicate occurrences. No prepared capacity, matrix, demand or vertex heap is supplied. The represented typed graph domain, complete solver composition, degenerate outer dispatch and full-paper runtime remain separate.",
